Hi Luiz,

sorry for the late response. Here are my answers and the bluez debug 
logging file.

For this logfile I had paired to a bluetooth keyboard 
(F2:40:18:84:AC:3A). The pairing agent had show me the passkey to enter, 
but I have typed a wrong one into the keyboard. After a couple of 
seconds the agent show me a new pass key. I had typed in the correct 
passkey and the keyboard has paired successfully in the background. But 
the pass key window stays forever on the screen. I guess bluez haven't 
called a paring complete method or something.

Other answers to your questions are in the quoting.


Best Regards
Björn

On 08/04/2018 07:00 AM, Luiz Augusto von Dentz wrote:
> Hi Bjorn,
>
> On Fri, Aug 3, 2018 at 5:15 PM, Björn Hauffe <bjoern@64b.de> wrote:
>> Hello Folks,
>>
>> i hope this is the right place to report this bug. If i try to pair a
>> Bluetooth 4.0 Keyboard with the bluez daemon and the first try wasn't
>> successful, the successful try after that won't displayed by the registered
>> bluetooth Agent (e.g. GUI). The Pin is still displayed by the Bluetooth tool
>> forever. I think the problem is, that the registered reply method is never
>> called by the bluez daemon (over  D-Bus).
> I guess you are talking about the method call not reply here, do you
> have the daemon logs when that happens? Perhaps you are saying the the
> daemon never calls Cancel so the agent stay in DisplayPasskey forever?
i mean the daemon never calls "complete" after the second try, so the 
agent will stay in DisplayPasskey forever.
>> Tested with Bluetooth GUI tool from Ubuntu 18.04.1 and Fedora 28 (Bluez
>> 5.49). Also tested with a self written D-Bus based pairing agent.
>>
>> My hardware for testing: Logitech K850, Microsoft Designer Keyboard
>>
>>
>> Steps to reproduce:
>>
>> 1. made a pairing try with a bluetooth 4.0 Keyboard, but let it fail (wrong
>> pin for example)
>>
>> 2. the second pin will displayed by the bluetooth tool
>>
>> 3. enter the new displayed pin correct to successful finish the pairing
>> process
>>
>> 4. you can't see that the pairing process is finish, because the GUI will
>> not show any feedback.
> What feedback do you expect here, that Paired is set to true?
I expect that the passkey window will be closed, because the pairing was 
successful completed by bluez.
>
>> 5. open bluetoothctl and check that the keyboard is paired.
> Does the keyboard pairs or not?
The Keyboard is paired, so i can use it. The Problem is that the Pairing 
agent will show the pairing key forever.
>
>> If i miss something, please let me know.
>>
>>
>> Best regards
>>
>> Björn
